        symbolImages: {
            type: 'array', displayName: 'Symbol Images', group: 'Data',
            // ─── AN UNSET CONNECTION MUST NOT ERASE A CONFIGURED LIST ───────────────
            // (2026-08-10) Observed in a real project: the reels rendered as empty cells and
            // pressing Spin did nothing visible, on a graph that was otherwise perfect —
            // Stage > 5 ReelColumn > 3 ReelCell each, correct symbol paths, assets serving 200.
            //
            // The controller's own `symbolImages` parameter held the three paths. But the
            // component ALSO wires `Component Inputs.symbolImages -> ReelController.symbolImages`,
            // and the page placing the instance passed nothing (its instance carried only
            // width/height/flex, and zero connections). So the input resolved empty, this setter
            // wrote [] over the good paths, and `_assignInitialSymbols` exits on its first line:
            //     if (!_i.symbolImages || _i.symbolImages.length === 0) return;
            // No sprite is ever created. Spin still runs the whole maths chain — it just has
            // nothing to draw, which is why the screen does not change.
            //
            // It also explains why the same component rendered on one mount path and not
            // another: where the connection never fires, the parameter survives; where it fires
            // with an unset input, it is destroyed. Same graph, opposite outcome.
