                // 2026-06-15 (trace 1781514456452): every other layout-affecting
                // setter (column0..N, centerGrid, fitMode, fitPadding) routes through
                // the layout machinery — this one only stored the flag. When autoLayout
                // flipped true AFTER the columns wired (input order is not guaranteed on
                // project/editor load), the column setters' _maybeAutoLayout calls had
                // already early-bailed (autoLayout was still false at L572), and turning
                // it on here armed NOTHING — neither the next-tick retry loop nor the
                // stage-resize listener (both live inside _maybeAutoLayout). So layout
                // ran only once, unguarded, at first spin; if the stage was unsized at
                // that instant the grid pinned top-left and never re-spread until a hard
                // refresh. Schedule layout when it turns on (no-op when false; the retry
                // loop is re-entry-safe — it clearTimeout-dedups and no-ops with 0 cols).
                if (this._internal.autoLayout) {
                    this._maybeAutoLayout();
