        // (2026-08-13, user: "for most slots the icons are touching with no spacing … but that is
        // not what is happening in our pixi slot … it takes me ages to make them without spacing")
        //
        // The two gaps were owned by different nodes. Horizontal (columnPadding) lives here, on the
        // node a user actually edits. VERTICAL (cellPadding) lived ONLY on PixiReelColumn — and
        // _applyAutoLayout pushed cellWidth/cellHeight/visibleRows down to every column but never
        // this. So closing the vertical gaps on a 5-reel slot meant opening five separate column
        // nodes and zeroing the same number five times, and any later autoLayout pass left them
        // alone (it never wrote the port), so nothing warned you when one column was missed.
