        // (parent._xgeniaStageWidth) is populated by PixiStage.registerAppRef
        // on a DIFFERENT async lifecycle event than the column setters that
        // schedule this. If the 50ms timer won that race, stageW===0,
        // _applyAutoLayout skipped the centering branches, the grid pinned to
        // top-left — and nothing rescheduled, so it stayed broken until a hard
        // refresh (or an unrelated input, e.g. the spin) re-fired this AFTER
        // the stage tag was set. That ordering-luck is the entire bug.
