name: 'Cascade The Reels',
docs: 'https://docsapp.xgenia.com/nodes/slot-games/cascade-the-reels',
// (2026-09-04, export 1788429855009 — "GemCascade") The compiled doc for this node had no
// description at all, and the system prompt said "**Cascading / tumble**: insert `Cascade
// The Reels` between Weighted Reels and Check Wins". The build did exactly that: it wired
// WeightedReels:reels -> Cascade:reels, drove Cascade:Do from a 350ms Timer, and never fed
// Cascade's own `reels` output back into its input — so every beat re-cascaded the ORIGINAL
// spin grid. A tumble that cannot progress. It also read this node as a cluster FINDER; it
// is a REMOVER (see doCascade: the only thing that decides what clears is
// winningLinesDetails). The description below is what the model reads (regenerated at ship
// Step 0.5); the generator reads ONE string literal per member. Nothing behavioural changed.
description: 'Tumble/cascade REMOVER + REFILL. It does NOT find wins and has no adjacency or cluster logic of its own: it clears ONLY the cells named in `winningLinesDetails`, drops the survivors down each column, refills the gaps from the top (weighted by `symbolWeights`, seeded from `Seeds` when wired) and emits the new grid on `reels`. Fed no winningLinesDetails it clears NOTHING and still fires Done, so a silent no-op looks like a working cascade. `winningLinesDetails` shape: an array of objects, and only `positions` is read, as [row, col] pairs — ROW FIRST, the opposite order from Check Wins customPaylines ([col,row]) — e.g. [{ positions: [[2,0],[3,0],[2,1]], payout: 40 }]. {row, col} objects work too; out-of-range or other shapes are skipped in silence. Calculate Winnings:winningLinesDetails and Reel Ways Calculate Winnings:winningLinesDetails already emit this; Check Wins:winningLines does NOT (no positions), so wiring that in clears nothing. THE LOOP CONTRACT, and the part builds keep getting wrong: the grid is STATE. Hold it in a Variable2, wire that variable into `reels`, and write the `reels` output of this node BACK to the same variable each pass (Cascade.reels -> SetVariable -> Variable2 -> Cascade.reels). Wiring Weighted Reels:reels straight into `reels` gives a cascade that re-runs the original spin on every beat and never progresses. The WIN EVALUATOR and the DISPLAY must both read that same variable, or the maths scores a grid the player never saw. FIRING: one Do per evaluation pass, after the winningLinesDetails for that pass have been computed; the chain ends on the pass that pays nothing.',
