docs: 'https://docsapp.xgenia.com/nodes/slot-games/check-wins',
// (2026-09-04, export 1788429855009 — "GemCascade", asked for cluster pays + cascading
// tumble) The compiled doc for this node carried input/output CODE dumps and NO prose at
// all, so the only way to learn that Check Wins means FIXED PAYLINES was to read this
// file. The system prompt meanwhile said "**Cluster pays**: use `Check Wins` with cluster
// logic in a JS function", which reads as "Check Wins is how you do clusters". The model
// spent 15 search_node_source_code calls, wired Check Wins → Calculate Winnings, and
// shipped twenty fixed 5-of-a-kind paylines over 15 of the 49 visible cells while telling
// the user it had built cluster pays. There is no adjacency or flood-fill code anywhere in
// this file, or in cascade-the-reels.js, or anywhere in the node library.
//
// The description strings below are what compiled-node-docs / inspect_node /
// list_available_nodes hand the model (the docs regenerate from this file at ship —
// Step 0.5). The generator reads ONE string literal per member, so each stays a single
