description: 'Scores FIXED PAYLINES on a spun grid. Reads `reels` as columns-of-rows (reels[col][row]) and, for each payline, walks the cells that line names looking for `minConsecutiveSymbols`+ of the same symbol from the LEFT, with `wildSymbol` matching anything. With `customPaylines` unwired it uses a BUILT-IN table of twenty 5-long lines across COLUMNS 0-4 on ROWS 0-2 ONLY — on any grid that is not 5x3 it scores just those 15 cells and silently ignores every other cell (a 7x7 grid: 15 of 49). `customPaylines` is Array<Array<[col,row]>> and can express any fixed SHAPE (V, zigzag, a hand-listed lattice), but a payline is an ORDERED list of cells, so this node has NO notion of a connected same-symbol group. IT DOES NOT DO CLUSTER PAYS, adjacency, flood fill, or scatter-anywhere pays — there is no such code in this file and no other node in the library evaluates them either; write that in a JS function. Output `winningLines` is [[lineNumber, [symbols...]], ...] and carries NO CELL POSITIONS, so it cannot be wired into Cascade The Reels:winningLinesDetails (which needs positions and would clear nothing) — positions come from Calculate Winnings:winningLinesDetails. FIRING: Weighted Reels.Done -> Do, with the same grid on `reels`; scoring is deferred to after inputs settle, and it fires Done even on error (with empty winningLines).',
