docs: 'https://docsapp.xgenia.com/nodes/slot-games/spin-calculate',
// ─── THE FREE-SPIN CONTRACT (2026-09-04, export 1788429855009 — "GemCascade") ──────────
// `isCascadingInProgress` (doCalculation, below) is the only thing standing between a
// cascading slot and a game that costs nothing to play, and NOTHING outside this file said
// so: the compiled doc for this node carried input/output code dumps and no description.
//
// That build set cascadingReelsEnabled: true, fed `spinWinnings` from a `cascadeWinTotal`
// ACCUMULATOR Variable2, and fired `Do` ONLY from the settle branch of a Condition
// (HasWin.onfalse). At settle the accumulator holds the whole chain total, so on EVERY
// winning spin spinWinnings > 0, isCascadingInProgress was true, and the bet was never
// deducted, `hits` never incremented and `spinCount` never advanced. Winning spins were
// free, with real payouts, in a build the completion gate certified.
//
// What the flag was written to mean: "this call is a mid-cascade payout, not the spin
// itself". It only means that when `spinWinnings` is THIS PASS's win. Which gives the
// contract in the description below, and one structural dead end worth naming here:
// `hits++` needs spinWinnings > 0 AND !isCascadingInProgress, i.e. spinWinnings > 0 AND
// NOT (cascadingReelsEnabled AND spinWinnings > 0) — so with cascading enabled `hits` can
// NEVER increment, whatever the wiring. That is a logic hole in this node, not a wiring
// mistake; it is documented rather than changed because live games read `hits` and a
// behaviour change here needs an editor/viewer rebuild to reach anyone.
//
// The description strings are what compiled-node-docs / inspect_node / list_available_nodes
// hand the model (regenerated from this file at ship — Step 0.5). The generator reads ONE
// string literal per member, so each stays a single literal. Nothing behavioural changed.
description: 'Per-spin bank: takes the previous capital / totalBets / totalWinnings / spinCount / hits, applies this spin and emits the new values. CASCADING CHANGES WHO PAYS FOR THE SPIN — read this before wiring a tumble game. Internally: isCascadingInProgress = cascadingReelsEnabled AND spinWinnings > 0, and the bet deduction, the hits increment and the spinCount increment are ALL skipped while that is true. So with cascadingReelsEnabled true the bet is charged ONLY on a call where spinWinnings reads 0. Two rules follow and breaking either makes the game FREE TO PLAY at full payout: (1) `spinWinnings` must be the win of THIS evaluation pass — wire Calculate Winnings:spinWinnings (or the per-pass payout of your own evaluator) directly. NEVER wire a running total or an accumulator Variable2: at settle an accumulated total is greater than zero on every winning spin, the node reads that as "a cascade is still in progress", and no bet is ever deducted. (2) It must FIRE on the pass that pays NOTHING — that zero-winnings call is the only one that charges the bet and advances spinCount. Triggering it only from the win branch of a Condition, or only from the settle branch while its winnings input still holds the chain total, means the charge call never happens. With cascadingReelsEnabled false the node bills once per Do, which is what a non-cascading slot wants. Also note `hits` is unreachable while cascadingReelsEnabled is true (the increment requires spinWinnings > 0 and NOT isCascadingInProgress, which cannot both hold) — count hit rate outside this node. FIRING: Calculate Winnings.Done -> Do, then Done -> Spin Result.Do.',
